    "done_when": "A new test, tests/test_resume_sweep_needs_an_observed_death.py, builds three wait-met runs in a temporary crew home and runs the sweep once: one whose supervisor recorded an exit (lifted), one whose checked pid on this host is found dead (lifted), one whose liveness is unknown because its launcher_host is another host with no exit record (not lifted, with the reason naming unknown liveness). A fourth case holds a proven-live local process and is not lifted, as today. The unknown-liveness case fails at the base revision because it is lifted (logged) and passes at the head. The negative control, in a scratch copy, restores the guard that refuses only a proven-live process; the unknown-liveness case fails, with the mutation on the red log's first line and an EXIT= line after pytest's output. The gate is the new test plus the existing test files that exercise the resume sweep; both arms are recorded as one JSON object each under baseline_suite and after_suite (revision, command, exit_status, one log_path, failure_ids), each log ending in an EXIT= line, with the head arm adding no failing id. ruff check plus ruff format --check on the changed paths add no finding against the base. The tests neither read nor write the real ~/.config/reckon, and start no process they do not terminate.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
    "goal": "Plan a-stalled-row-says-whether-the-worker-lives, followup f-asrswtwl-sweep-guard-needs-observed-death: the resume sweep lifts a run only once its process is observed to have ended. Read the followup in docs/plans/a-stalled-row-says-whether-the-worker-lives.html. The wait-met row tells the reader the sweep lifts a run only after an observed end, but the sweep's only process guard (reckon/crew/resumption.py near :596) refuses a proven-live process and nothing else, so a run whose liveness is unknown is resumed as though dead, which may duplicate a live worker. Make the sweep require an observed death before resuming: a checked pid found dead on this host, or a supervisor-recorded exit, using the vocabulary §3 landed (the host-gated reading merged at 8413ce50) rather than a new one. A run of unknown liveness is left in place with its reason named.",
